AL_API_KEY` in the macOS Keychain by running `/usr/bin/security`. The sandbox profile `agent.sb` denies that exec, so it fails with `EPERM`. Vibe doesn't catch that error, so the process exits with status 2 before any model request. I reproduced this inside the same sandbox profile.\n\n**Fix:** `run-vibe.sh` now passes `VIBE_TEST_DISABLE_KEYRING=1` into the sandboxed environment. Vibe then skips every Keychain read. I left `agent.sb` alone rather than allowing `/usr/bin/security`, since that would let the agent reach the Keychain client.\n\n**Verification:** I re-ran the script with a dummy key. It now gets past startup and fails only at OpenRouter's auth check, as expected for an invalid key. I did not make a real model call, so a run with your real key is still untested. I restored the tracked `logs/last-run.*` files to the original failure logs afterwards.\n\n**Caveat:** The variable name says \"TEST\", but Vibe reads it in production code. If a future Vibe release renames it, the Keychain error will come back. The reproduction in `ANSWER.md` will show it.\n\nChanges are uncommitted: `run-vibe.sh` modified, `ANSWER.md` added.","ttft_ms":1899,"type":"result","duration_ms":74416,"uuid":"b7c515f5-f8f1-4796-9b0f-86bb35383be3","ttft_stream_ms":1706,"time_to_request_ms":213,"first_content_frame_ms":1706,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":36,"outputTokens":9711,"cacheReadInputTokens":611018,"cacheCreationInputTokens":30317,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.01703268,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":3768,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":30317,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T22:27:53.817Z"}
